I'll implement the PER-324 story from the story file and code context, starting by reading both so the changes stay inside that scope.
The story is a backend validation fix for rating stars. I'll look at the rating service, view model, and how this app already returns validation errors.
Star values are stored with no range check, so a rating of 0 or 99 can be saved and pulled into the product average. I'll enforce 1–5 in the view model and in `createRating` before anything is written.
Validation is in place before the write. Next I’ll add the boundary tests and confirm invalid stars stay out of the average.
The rating module targets Java 25. I'll run its unit tests with that JDK.
Creating a rating now rejects any star value outside 1–5 before it is saved, and the product average counts only ratings inside that range.

- `RatingPostVm` requires `star` to be from 1 to 5 (`@Min` / `@Max`, message `must be between 1 and 5`).
- `RatingService.createRating` runs that validation before any repository call. A failure throws `ConstraintViolationException`, which the existing handler returns as HTTP 400 with `statusCode` `400 BAD_REQUEST`, title `Bad Request`, detail `Request information is not valid`, and a `star` field error.
- The average query includes only stars from 1 to 5, so values such as 0 or 99 do not affect the average.

